WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.220
Ground, ocean, ice:
every surface radiates,

2
00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:06.590
simply because of its own temperature.

3
00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:11.070
The hotter a surface gets, the more
power it sends out as infrared.

4
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:13.500
Picture a planet soaking up sunlight.

5
00:00:13.550 --> 00:00:18.620
It warms and radiates more, until
what it emits matches what it absorbs.

6
00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:21.630
Earth absorbs a steady stream of sunlight.

7
00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.400
How warm must it get before
it radiates all of that away?

8
00:00:25.450 --> 00:00:29.750
In this mission, you'll meet
emissivity: how well a surface radiates,

9
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.090
compared with a perfect black body.

10
00:00:32.140 --> 00:00:35.480
Then you'll split Earth into
a surface and an atmosphere,

11
00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:38.530
and balance the energy
flowing through each layer.

12
00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:43.010
Your mission: calculate the temperature
at which a planet radiates away all the

13
00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:44.510
sunlight it absorbs.
